    "summary": "A man&#039;s hat, so-called &#039;four-winds&#039;, worn during summer.  Four large blue points stitched to a red base with blue trim.  Both fabrics made of commercially woven wool cloth.  A strip of yellow cloth included in seam securing two sections together and in one of the vertical seams in the red base.  Lined with cotton printed tabby woven fabric: two repeating small-scale motifs on an aubergine coloured ground.  Stuffed with down.",
